# 🛠️ Forge-Lite SDK

Welcome to **Forge-Lite**, a lightweight graphics framework written in C. This SDK bundles native window management and modern OpenGL rendering into a small, self-contained pipeline for 2D graphics and simple games.

---

## 📦 What's Inside the SDK Folder

Once compiled, this SDK distributes two primary components:
* **`Forge-Lite.h`** — The public header with API declarations you include in your source files.
* **`libforge_lite.a`** — The monolithic static library archive containing the engine implementation.

---

## 📋 API Function Reference

| Function Signature | Description | Return Value / Behavior |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `void init(int width, int height, const char* title)` | Creates a native OS window, initializes the graphics context and shaders, and configures a 2D projection scaled to pixel coordinates. | No return value. Call once before any drawing or input polling. |
| `int window_is_open(void)` | Checks whether the application window is still open. | Returns `1` if the window is open, `0` if the user has closed the window. |
| `void update_screen(void)` | Presents the backbuffer to the display, updates the internal delta time, polls input and window events, and clears the screen for the next frame. | No return value. Call once per frame. |
| `void setBackgroundColor(Color color)` | Sets the clear/background color used when the screen is cleared each frame. | No return value. |
| `float getDeltaTime(void)` | Returns the elapsed time in seconds between the previous frame and the current frame. | Returns a `float` (e.g., `0.016` for ~60 FPS). |
| `Texture loadTexture(const char* filepath)` | Loads an image file from disk into GPU memory as a 2D texture. Supported file formats depend on the build (common: PNG, JPG). | Returns a `Texture` struct with a valid `id` on success, or an empty/zeroed `Texture` (e.g., `id == 0`) on failure. |
| `void drawShape(ShapeType type, Color color, Texture texture, float x, float y, float width, float height)` | Draws a geometric primitive (rectangle, circle, etc.). Provide either a `color` OR a `texture` — supplying both or neither is undefined. Coordinates use window pixel space. | No return value. |
| `void drawImage(Texture texture, float x, float y, float width, float height)` | Draws a textured quad. Pass `0` for `width` and/or `height` to use the texture's original dimensions. | No return value. |
| `int isKeyDown(int key)` | Returns whether the specified keyboard key is currently pressed. The function normalizes lowercase letter codes to uppercase. | Returns `1` if pressed, `0` otherwise. |
| `void getMousePosition(float* x, float* y)` | Writes the mouse cursor position (in window pixel coordinates) into the provided float pointers. | No return value. Make sure pointers are valid. |
| `int isMouseButtonDown(int button)` | Checks the state of a mouse button. | Returns `1` if held down, `0` if released. Button mapping: `0` = left, `1` = right, `2` = middle (if supported). |
| `int checkCollision(Rectangle r1, Rectangle r2)` | Tests whether two axis-aligned rectangles overlap. | Returns `1` if the rectangles intersect, `0` otherwise. |
| `Rectangle getShapeBounds(ShapeType type, float x, float y, float width, float height)` | Computes an axis-aligned bounding `Rectangle` for a given shape and parameters. | Returns a `Rectangle` struct representing the bounds in window coordinates. |
| `void shutdown_framework(void)` | Tears down graphics resources, destroys the window, and performs library cleanup. | No return value. Call before exiting your program. |

---

## 🚀 Compilation Blueprint

### 1. Project Layout

To build a program that uses the compiled SDK assets, place your source file next to the library files:

```text
your_project/
├── Forge-Lite.h
├── libforge_lite.a
└── main.c
```

### 2. Compilation Command (Windows with GCC)

Open a terminal in your project folder and run:

```bash
gcc main.c libforge_lite.a -lgdi32 -lwinmm -o game.exe
```

(Optional) Example for Linux (may require different link flags depending on build):

```bash
gcc main.c libforge_lite.a -lGL -lX11 -lpthread -o game
```

---

## 🔧 For Core Contributors & Developers

If you are contributing to the Forge-Lite engine itself, use the CMake configuration to rebuild the static library and test applications:

```bash
# Create a fresh build directory and configure the project
cmake -S . -B build

# Build the library and executables (Debug or Release)
cmake --build build --config Debug
```

Notes:
* The SDK header (`Forge-Lite.h`) documents the public API types (`Color`, `Texture`, `ShapeType`, `Rectangle`, etc.). Refer to it for exact struct and enum definitions.
* Report issues or feature requests via the repository issue tracker.

